# =============================================================================
# fragilis — Rejected flaky test modifier
# =============================================================================
#
# What this teaches:
#   • `faber test` rejects a case with `fragilis <N>` before executing its body.
#     The runner does not execute flaky retries.
#   • `fragilis` is not an allow-failure modifier and does not retry a case.
#
# Common mistakes:
#   • Expecting `fragilis <N>` to allow failure or retry a test — `faber test`
#     rejects it because flaky retries are not implemented.
# =============================================================================

# fragilis — rejected flaky test modifier
#
# GRAMMAR:
#   testModifier :← 'fragilis' integer
#
# EXPECTED RUNNER OUTCOME:
#   `faber test corpus/fragilis/fragilis.fab` rejects this case; its body is
#   not executed. The failure explains that flaky retries are not executed.
#
# BACKEND:
#   declaration-only test modifier (whitelist: fragilis/fragilis.fab).
#

test "fragilis is rejected" flaky 1 {
    assert true
}
